BT /F1 8 Tf 0.45 0.55 0.65 rg 50 812.89 Td (MODULAR BMS ENGINE - DESIGN & SCALABILITY REPORT) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 0.45 0.55 0.65 rg 460 812.89 Td (ISO 26262 / ASIL-D) Tj ET
0.059 0.090 0.165 rg
BT /F2 15 Tf 50.00 770.00 Td (3. Mathematical Formulations & Algorithmic Design) Tj ET
0.008 0.518 0.780 rg
50.00 765.00 495.00 2.00 re f
0.012 0.412 0.631 rg
BT /F2 11 Tf 50.00 745.00 Td (3.1 Single-Pass O\(N\) Extrema Identification) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50.00 731.00 Td (Given an array of cell voltages V = [v0, v1, ..., vN-1], the engine traverses the array exactly once:) Tj ET
0.945 0.961 0.976 rg
50.00 673.00 495.00 40.00 re f
0.796 0.835 0.882 rg
50.00 673.00 495.00 40.00 re S
0.059 0.090 0.165 rg
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 70.00 697.00 Td (Weakest Cell:   k_min = arg min \(v_i\),      V_min = v_k_min) Tj ET
0.059 0.090 0.165 rg
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 70.00 683.00 Td (Strongest Cell: k_max = arg max \(v_i\),      V_max = v_k_max) Tj ET
0.012 0.412 0.631 rg
BT /F2 9.5 Tf 70.00 669.00 Td (Imbalance: Delta V_raw = V_max - V_min,     V_pack = Sum\(v_i\),  V_avg = floor\(V_pack / N\)) Tj ET
0.012 0.412 0.631 rg
BT /F2 11 Tf 50.00 658.00 Td (3.2 The Flaw of Fixed Imbalance Thresholds) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50.00 644.00 Td (Typical BMS architectures trip an alarm when Delta V > V_fixed \(e.g. 30 mV\). This causes severe faults:) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 9 Tf 65.00 630.00 Td (1. Non-linear OCV Knees: Below 20% SoC and above 80% SoC, dV/dSoC spikes by an order of magnitude.) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 9 Tf 65.00 618.00 Td (   A normal 2% cell capacity difference produces ~1 mV at 50% SoC, but 60 to 90 mV below 15% SoC!) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 9 Tf 65.00 606.00 Td (2. Dynamic IR Drop Divergence: Cell internal resistance varies by +/- 5% to 10% across manufacturing.) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 9 Tf 65.00 594.00 Td (   Under a 40A discharge burst, a Delta R of 1.5 mOhm causes a dynamic voltage split of 40A * 1.5mOhm = 60 mV.) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 9 Tf 65.00 582.00 Td (   This split collapses back to 0 mV when current stops; balancing against it ruins pack equilibrium.) Tj ET
0.012 0.412 0.631 rg
BT /F2 11 Tf 50.00 562.00 Td (3.3 The Adaptive Imbalance Model Formulation) Tj ET
0.945 0.961 0.976 rg
50.00 498.00 495.00 50.00 re f
0.796 0.835 0.882 rg
50.00 498.00 495.00 50.00 re S
0.059 0.090 0.165 rg
BT /F2 10 Tf 70.00 530.00 Td (V_threshold\(SoC, I_pack\) = min\( V_base * gamma_SoC\(SoC\) + Delta V_IR\(I_pack\),  V_clamp_max \)) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 70.00 516.00 Td (Where: V_base = 25.0 mV,  gamma_max = 2.8x \(at 0% SoC\),  k_IR = 1.5 mV/A \(Discharge only\)) Tj ET
0.706 0.325 0.035 rg
BT /F2 8.5 Tf 70.00 502.00 Td (Safety Ceiling: V_clamp_max = 120.0 mV \(Ensures hardware micro-shorts are never masked\)) Tj ET
0.012 0.412 0.631 rg
BT /F2 11 Tf 50.00 483.00 Td (3.4 Temporal Imbalance Trend Filtering \(EMA + Numerical Derivative\)) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 9.5 Tf 50.00 469.00 Td (To reject inverter electrical noise \(+/- 2 to 5 mV\), the engine filters Delta V before computing the rate:) Tj ET
0.945 0.961 0.976 rg
50.00 411.00 495.00 40.00 re f
0.796 0.835 0.882 rg
50.00 411.00 495.00 40.00 re S
0.059 0.090 0.165 rg
BT /F2 9 Tf 70.00 435.00 Td (EMA Filter:       Delta V_filt\(k\) = alpha * Delta V_raw\(k\) + \(1 - alpha\) * Delta V_filt\(k-1\)  [alpha = 0.15]) Tj ET
0.012 0.412 0.631 rg
BT /F2 9 Tf 70.00 421.00 Td (Imbalance Rate:   d\(Delta V\)/dt = [Delta V_filt\(k\) - Delta V_filt\(k-1\)] / Delta t    \(mV/second\)) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 70.00 407.00 Td (Deadband Hysteresis: Candidate = INCREASING if rate > +0.25 mV/s; DECREASING if rate < -0.25 mV/s) Tj ET
0.200 0.255 0.333 rg
BT /F1 9 Tf 50.00 396.00 Td (A 5-cycle persistence counter locks the state, preventing chatter between INCREASING and DECREASING.) Tj ET
